## Residual risks (return)
| ID | Sev | Residual | Why not extra 2.9 FAIL |
|----|-----|----------|------------------------|
| R1 | **HIGH** | Check/LLVM/wasm later-arg after inner `RPAREN` (F1/F2) | **This is the 2.9 FAIL** — listed so peers do not lose it |
| R2 | HIGH | `emit-bc` skips the walker; `CALL println` gets SECRET | Backend wiring; walker never runs. Name; do not bury |
| R3 | MED | Stmt `println` ≠ `c_secret_emit_guard` (unify still OPEN) | Engineering of 2.9; emit-c belt still BLOCK on Z1/Z2 |
| R4 | MED | LLVM builtin `print` prints SECRET (`s71` R2) | `print` not a typed product API; check type-fails |
| R5 | MED | 2.10 user wrapper `leak(tok)` → `oo_print_str(x)` | Separate sprint |
| R6 | MED | 5.8 `${}` interp not implemented | Literal string; IDENT never reached the sink |
| R7 | LOW | Walker LPAREN-optional scan-forward (`let f = println` then later `foo(tok)`) | Accidental refuse / FP class, not a hide |
| R8 | LOW | Method `recv.println()` empty args skips `c_guard_scan_idents`; receiver untainted as sink arg | Not a product print lower |
| R9 | — | Full IFC / `#[Secret]` / interproc beyond `__fr_secret__` | `SECRET_TAINT.oot` — do not greenwash |
| R10 | — | 2.8 macro second pass | **Closed residual-doc**; do not reopen |

**Explicitly not residuals of this close:** T1 return/alias/if (smokes
green); T2 field/args/comment-FP (smokes green); 6.1 `env_set` (other
OWN; integration RED is check type-first, not println).

---

## What we do **not** claim
- 2.9 walker → `c_secret_emit_guard` is **implemented** (it is not).
- `oodac check` / `emit-llvm` / `emit-wasm` refuse every SECRET in a
  println argument list (Z2 they do not).
- `emit-bc` is a sealed SECRET backend.
- Full IFC / `#[Secret]` / `${}` / `__sec_sink__` wrappers.
- LLVM multi-arg println (builtin is first-arg only).
- Runtime `oo_print_*` redaction.

---

## Evidence commands (repro)
```text
OODAC=/home/jeryd/Projects/openOODA/ooda/oodac/oodac
cd ooda
OODAC_BIN=$OODAC bash scripts/s29_println_guard_smoke.oo
  # ALL OK (bare IDENT + string no-FP + eprintln IDENT)
$OODAC check  fixtures/secret_sink_fail.oo
  # ERR secret println sink refuses SECRET x   rc=1
$OODAC emit-c fixtures/secret_sink_fail.oo
  # same
# Z2 FN (ephemeral /tmp/s29_sec_1131649):
#   // SECRET: tok
#   println((n), tok)   and   println(id(1), tok)
$OODAC check     /tmp/s29_sec_1131649/06_group_later.oo   # OK rc=0   FN
$OODAC emit-c    /tmp/s29_sec_1131649/06_group_later.oo   # ERR secret tok  rc=1
$OODAC emit-llvm /tmp/s29_sec_1131649/06_group_later.oo   # rc=0  @oo_print_int only
$OODAC emit-wasm /tmp/s29_sec_1131649/06_group_later.oo   # rc=0  tok dropped
$OODAC emit-bc   /tmp/s29_sec_1131649/01_bare.oo          # rc=0  CALL println 1
```

Close criteria (Domain Expert; not this write):

1. Check-path println/eprintln walk is **depth-aware** **or** replaced
   by `c_secret_emit_guard` on lowered args.
2. Live 06/07/08/22 become dual-path `ERR\tsecret` (check + emit-c +
   emit-llvm + emit-wasm).
3. Stmt `println` may keep `c_emit_println` as a belt; unify is the
   **front-door**. Smoke must add a later-arg-after-RPAREN fixture.
4. emit-bc: wire the same front-door **or** keep R2 named fail-open.
5. Still **no** claim of full IFC / 2.8 expand / 2.10 wrappers.

